---
export const title = "Translate";
export const jsFile = "translate.js";
---

<h1>{title}</h1>

<div class="desc">
  This component takes a key value set between its opening and closing tags,
  matches that key to a JSON language file then outputs the value to the HTML.
  It is used in conjunction with the <a href="#Language%20Selector"
    >language selector</a
  > that allows users to change the display language.
  <br /><br />
</div>

<div class="demo-wrap">
  <rex-translate>welcome</rex-translate>
</div>
<h3>In Code</h3>
<div class="code-wrap">
  <pre><code class="usage language-javascript">{`
  // import the component
  import {rex-translate} from TBA;
  
  //use it in your HTML
  <rex-translate>welcome</rex-translate>
  `}</code></pre>
  <br />
  <section class="highlight">
    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <em class="alert"
      >This is a work in progress, future versions will not require manual
      editing or a downalod of the file</em
    >

    This componet requires some manual setup as it can accomodate any number of
    languages and translations. Editing of the <code>"translate.js"</code> script
    is a requirment for this one. Follow these steps (in the translate.js file):
    <div class="sub">
      <h4>① Install</h4>

      Download <a href="/translate.js" download="translate.js">translate.js</a>
      and place it in your apps filesystem, just like any other JS file.

      <h4>② Import <small>in JS where you want to use it</small></h4>
      <pre><code>{`
  import "idk where you saved it/translate.js"
      `}</code></pre>

      <h4>③ Customise <small>translate.js file</small></h4>
      At the top of the file are the imports for the language JSON files
      <br />
      <pre><code>{`
  import english from "../../translations/en.json";
  import japanese from "../../translations/ja.json";
  import french from "../../translations/fr.json";
        `}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  import "../lib/translate";
</script>
